{{!-- One section of the Playbook tab (D11): a panel headed by its bar, resting on what was chosen,
      with one door on the bar to everything on offer. Both are in the markup; the door slides one
      out and the other in (the Disclosure machinery the rail's groups use), and the sheet remembers
      which the reader left open. The book's instruction rides the bar only while choosing.

      Params: `section` (PlaybookSection), `title`, `note`, `index` (its bar's place on this tab),
      `rest` and `choose` — the partials that draw the two bodies, each handed these params — and
      whatever those two read (`data`, `cgContext`, …). Named partials rather than a `{{#> }}` block:
      Handlebars strips prototype access from partial-block content, silently. --}}
<section class="stonetop-panel stonetop-section" data-disclosure-row data-section="{{section.key}}">
	{{> "stonetop.bar" title=title index=index note=note noteWhileOpen=true
	    action=(ifThen section.hasDoor "stonetop.section-door" "")
	    controls=(sectionId @root.sheetIdPrefix section.key) door=section.door}}
	<div class="stonetop-section-rest" data-disclosure-shut>{{#if (and rest section.rests)}}{{> (lookup . "rest") .}}{{/if}}</div>
	{{#if section.hasDoor}}
	<div class="stonetop-section-choose" id="{{sectionId @root.sheetIdPrefix section.key}}" hidden>{{#if choose}}{{> (lookup . "choose") .}}{{/if}}</div>
	{{/if}}
</section>
